  "worked_solution": "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =k\\cdot k-27\\cdot 3 \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-81 & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =81 \\\\ k & =\\pm 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $k$ are $k=\\pm 9.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
